## 1. Control Overview

### 1.1 Control Statement
ASSET MONITORING AND TRACKING
Control: Employ tracking measures to monitor the location and movement of Emerald Retail assets within Emerald Retail designated control zones.
Discussion: Asset location technologies can help ensure that critical assets—including vehicles, equipment, and system components—remain in authorized locations. Organizations consult with the Office of the General Counsel and senior agency official for privacy regarding the deployment and use of asset location technologies to address potential privacy concerns.
Related Controls: CM-8, PE-16, PM-8.
Control Enhancements: None.
References: None.

### 1.2 Control Intent
The security control is establishing a set of rules pertaining to asset protection. In this case, it's for tracking asset location and movement of company devices that are to stay within designated zones. This is to satisfy control PE-20 and remain compliant under NIST 800-53 standards.

| Objective | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| Primary | Monitor and track devices |
| Secondary | Security logs showing breach in compliance |
| Compliance | Maintain 800-53 compliance with supporting artifacts |

### 1.3 Current Implementation
Currently, the company uses the software known as NinjaOne. This provides asset tracking to endpoint management, tracking assets in real time.
SOC alerts are configured within the software to provide updates when the asset is unreachable or breaches the set geofence boundary.
This automates monitoring and has manual interaction for incident response.

